 # Supplementary Material — Periodic Review as Sampled Governance
 
-*Accompanies: "Governance latency: the delay, the clock, and the stability of periodically reviewed renewable resources."*
+*Accompanies: "Governance latency: the delay, the clock, and the stability of periodically reviewed renewable resources" (version 47).*
 
 This supplementary accompanies the main paper on sampled governance — a governance loop in which state observation and control update occur at discrete review times — and consolidates the supporting material that does not fit in the main text's flow. It carries thirteen bodies of material: a statement inventory (S1); the remaining proofs and identification results (S2); the epistemic-layer results on observation, information, and delayed information (S3); the case-screening records at full detail (S4); the ecosystem-context and toy-test record (S5); the distributive-layer detail (S6); the empirical hypotheses with their declared tests (S7); the reproducibility register (S8); the screen-sensitivity battery and stage-scan decomposition records (S9); and the T_r-ranked test record (S10); the sensitivity, F-grid, Neimark--Sacker, and alternative-band records (S11); the F-calibration, ADH cross-system, and precision-certificate records (S12); and the demoted technical detail (S13). Every item carries its evidentiary status on the line; none is stated above it.
 
